
# P1-B8C: the acceptance PAGE is generated by _p1b8c-visual-runner.js on every run and its
# content is whichever variant was rendered last. The EVIDENCE it produces is committed
# (docs/evidence/p1-b8c-acceptance/); the scratch page is not.
assets/tests/_p1b8c-acceptance.html
assets/tests/_p1b8c-frame-*.html

# P1-B8C-R2: the USER's raw Apps Script editor export. 240,126 characters of production row data —
# every price, every product name, every site listing. §4 of the round is explicit that the RAW log
# must not be committed; what IS committed is assets/tests/_p1b8c-r2-live-derived.js, the reduced and
# rehydrated sixty rows. The export is input evidence, kept outside version control.
assets/tools/p1b8c-r1a-editor-log.txt
assets/tools/p1b8c-r1a-editor-log.txt.txt

# S8-B3-R3-CP2M-R4-R2: the headless browser runners pass --user-data-dir into the evidence
# directory so each scenario gets a clean profile. The CAPTURE is committed; the profile is a
# throwaway Chrome install that is rewritten on every run and must never enter version control.
docs/evidence/**/.chrome-profile
docs/evidence/**/.chrome-profile-*

# PSB-DEMO-R1: the demo runner generates this page on every run and deletes it after.
assets/tests/_psb-demo-page.html

# PSB-DEMO-R2: the R2 runner page and its mutated UI copy, generated per run and deleted after.
assets/tests/_psb-demo-r2-page.html
assets/tests/_psb-r2-mutant-ui.js
assets/tests/_psb-demo-r3-page.html
assets/tests/_psb-demo-r3-page-synth.html
assets/tests/_psb-r3-before-*
